00:02:13.977 --> 00:02:17.127
"Stay MECE my friends"
indeed guys stay MECE

00:02:17.127 --> 00:02:18.440
and you will be fine.

00:02:18.440 --> 00:02:21.860
So let's now look into
what MECE actually means.

00:02:21.860 --> 00:02:23.230
MECE is an acronym

00:02:23.230 --> 00:02:27.880
standing for Mutually, Exclusive,
Collectively, Exhaustive.

00:02:27.880 --> 00:02:29.960
And if you do not directly
understand right now

00:02:29.960 --> 00:02:30.793
what this means,

00:02:30.793 --> 00:02:33.240
just wait a sec I'm going
to explain it for you.

00:02:33.240 --> 00:02:36.930
So, Mutually Exclusive
means that different parts,

00:02:36.930 --> 00:02:39.440
should not overlap, they
should be disjoined,

00:02:39.440 --> 00:02:41.990
they should be separate from each other.

00:02:41.990 --> 00:02:45.310
And Collectively Exhaustive
means that several parts

00:02:45.310 --> 00:02:49.420
together should again form
the total of larger thing.

00:02:49.420 --> 00:02:52.290
MECE therefore is a principle
that you should apply

00:02:52.290 --> 00:02:56.810
whenever you decompose or
disaggregate a larger thing

00:02:56.810 --> 00:02:58.710
into its sub parts.

00:02:58.710 --> 00:03:02.010
So whenever you break something
down into smaller parts,

00:03:02.010 --> 00:03:04.820
when you have a problem
you want to do decompose it

00:03:04.820 --> 00:03:07.030
into smaller sub problems,

00:03:07.030 --> 00:03:10.620
into smaller sub facets of a larger thing,

00:03:10.620 --> 00:03:13.320
then this MECE principle comes into play

00:03:13.320 --> 00:03:14.610
and as I already hinted,

00:03:14.610 --> 00:03:16.790
this is something that is
of course super relevant

00:03:16.790 --> 00:03:17.950
to the consulting world,

00:03:17.950 --> 00:03:20.070
or to business practitioners in general,

00:03:20.070 --> 00:03:23.240
because for them it is a daily
task to break down things,

00:03:23.240 --> 00:03:24.580
to simplify things.

00:03:24.580 --> 00:03:26.870
So let's make it now a bit more tangible

00:03:26.870 --> 00:03:29.060
by looking at a visual representation

00:03:29.060 --> 00:03:30.850
of a MECE decomposition.

00:03:30.850 --> 00:03:34.450
What you see here is the MECE
decomposition of a circle.

00:03:34.450 --> 00:03:36.470
So let's imagine that you are tasked

00:03:36.470 --> 00:03:39.760
to break down a circle
into its sub components.

00:03:39.760 --> 00:03:42.430
And if you do it in the
way that is shown here,

00:03:42.430 --> 00:03:45.583
this decomposition would
meet the MECE principle

00:03:45.583 --> 00:03:48.560
because the sub parts
are mutually exclusive

00:03:48.560 --> 00:03:50.190
and collectively exhaustive.

00:03:50.190 --> 00:03:51.930
They are mutually exclusive

00:03:51.930 --> 00:03:54.180
because the parts do not overlap

00:03:54.180 --> 00:03:57.490
as you can see all the parts
are disjoined from each other

00:03:57.490 --> 00:03:59.840
and they are indeed
collectively exhaustive

00:03:59.840 --> 00:04:02.030
because if you take
all the parts together,

00:04:02.030 --> 00:04:05.950
the sum of them indeed
composes again a full circle.

00:04:05.950 --> 00:04:07.910
So maybe that sounds a bit complicated,

00:04:07.910 --> 00:04:11.130
but the truth is that
MECE is no rocket science.

00:04:11.130 --> 00:04:12.680
It is not really complicated,

00:04:12.680 --> 00:04:13.890
but it is rather something

00:04:13.890 --> 00:04:17.290
that we are all very familiar
with in our daily life.

00:04:17.290 --> 00:04:18.123
And for instance,

00:04:18.123 --> 00:04:20.820
you will absolutely naturally
follow the MECE principle

00:04:20.820 --> 00:04:23.990
if you would organize a
physical card collection.

00:04:23.990 --> 00:04:26.910
When I was a young kid, I
used to collect magic cards.

00:04:26.910 --> 00:04:29.823
It's a trading card game where
you can get lots of cards

00:04:29.823 --> 00:04:32.280
so that you can then
exchange with friends,

00:04:32.280 --> 00:04:34.450
where you then can also play
games against each other.

00:04:34.450 --> 00:04:35.440
Over my childhood,

00:04:35.440 --> 00:04:38.970
I collected hundreds if not
thousands of these cards.

00:04:38.970 --> 00:04:39.803
And as you can see,

00:04:39.803 --> 00:04:42.560
they're ordered and
they are indeed ordered

00:04:42.560 --> 00:04:44.060
by the color of the cards.

00:04:44.060 --> 00:04:46.330
So in this specific trading card game,

00:04:46.330 --> 00:04:48.030
cards had a distinct color,

00:04:48.030 --> 00:04:49.860
and I hope that you realize

00:04:49.860 --> 00:04:52.630
that by ordering the cards in this way,

00:04:52.630 --> 00:04:56.900
I was already following the
MECE principle at that time.

00:04:56.900 --> 00:04:58.400
But why is it MECE?

00:04:58.400 --> 00:05:01.490
And well let's look at the
first part Mutually Exclusive.

00:05:01.490 --> 00:05:04.590
If you put all your cards
into different groups,

00:05:04.590 --> 00:05:06.670
into different pockets of cards.

00:05:06.670 --> 00:05:09.600
Now in this example,
the colors of the cards.

00:05:09.600 --> 00:05:13.350
Then you put each card exactly
once into one of the pockets,

00:05:13.350 --> 00:05:15.440
and then this is mutually exclusive

00:05:15.440 --> 00:05:17.970
because these pockets
do not overlap, right?

00:05:17.970 --> 00:05:20.870
Because one card cannot be
in more than one pocket.

00:05:20.870 --> 00:05:24.350
But then of course it's
also collectively exhaustive

00:05:24.350 --> 00:05:26.350
because if every card has a color

00:05:26.350 --> 00:05:28.840
and you can assign every card to a pocket,

00:05:28.840 --> 00:05:30.350
then in the end all the cards

00:05:30.350 --> 00:05:32.570
we'll be distributed across the pockets,

00:05:32.570 --> 00:05:34.620
so this is then fine all
the cards would be gone,

00:05:34.620 --> 00:05:36.150
all the cards would be ordered.

00:05:36.150 --> 00:05:37.743
So yes, such a card collection

00:05:37.743 --> 00:05:41.320
will then be mutually exclusive
and collectively exhaustive,

00:05:41.320 --> 00:05:43.440
It will be MECE so as you can see,

00:05:43.440 --> 00:05:45.530
it is indeed no rocket science,

00:05:45.530 --> 00:05:48.770
but something that even many
kids will be able to do.

00:05:48.770 --> 00:05:51.600
So I hope it is clear now
what MECE actually means,

00:05:51.600 --> 00:05:53.210
but now let's get practical

00:05:53.210 --> 00:05:55.100
and let's jump in an example

00:05:55.100 --> 00:05:58.820
of how you can apply the MECE
principle to your daily work.

00:05:58.820 --> 00:06:00.850
So let's imagine the following scenario,

00:06:00.850 --> 00:06:03.510
you are working on a cost cutting project,

00:06:03.510 --> 00:06:04.580
either as a consultant

00:06:04.580 --> 00:06:07.480
or maybe also as an internal
employee in the company,

00:06:07.480 --> 00:06:09.530
and your objective that
you've been tasked with,

00:06:09.530 --> 00:06:10.990
by your senior management

00:06:10.990 --> 00:06:13.410
is to size the cost reduction potential

00:06:13.410 --> 00:06:15.670
for the client and to develop measures,

00:06:15.670 --> 00:06:17.640
to implement the cost reductions.

00:06:17.640 --> 00:06:19.037
So the management pretty
much wants to know,

00:06:19.037 --> 00:06:22.017
"Okay, roughly how much
cost can I take out

00:06:22.017 --> 00:06:23.567
"of different parts of the business,

00:06:23.567 --> 00:06:25.107
"and then what do I actually need to do,

00:06:25.107 --> 00:06:27.257
"what other measures do I actually achieve

00:06:27.257 --> 00:06:28.480
"these cost savings?"

00:06:28.480 --> 00:06:31.470
So you agreed on looking
into four concrete areas.

00:06:31.470 --> 00:06:34.740
This is the production,
the sales function,

00:06:34.740 --> 00:06:37.330
the purchasing function
and overhead, right?

00:06:37.330 --> 00:06:40.330
And for each of these areas,
now you size the potential,

00:06:40.330 --> 00:06:42.740
by doing some benchmarks
and some other things,

00:06:42.740 --> 00:06:45.080
you define some low hanging fruits,

00:06:45.080 --> 00:06:46.970
and then on top of that you identified

00:06:46.970 --> 00:06:48.660
more medium terms measures,

00:06:48.660 --> 00:06:50.890
now after identifying
all of this, you know,

00:06:50.890 --> 00:06:53.650
drafted a project plan
for the implementation.

00:06:53.650 --> 00:06:55.620
Now let's imagine you are an associate

00:06:55.620 --> 00:06:56.870
working on this project

00:06:56.870 --> 00:06:59.260
or as I said just a general
employee task with this

00:06:59.260 --> 00:07:02.310
and now your project leader
asks you to create an outline

00:07:02.310 --> 00:07:05.140
for the progress report of this project.

00:07:05.140 --> 00:07:07.180
And now I want you to pause the video

00:07:07.180 --> 00:07:10.290
and think for a second,
based on these information,

00:07:10.290 --> 00:07:13.420
if you would need to
draft a table of contents

00:07:13.420 --> 00:07:16.050
for such a report, how
would that look like?

00:07:16.050 --> 00:07:18.810
And let's now look into
two example outlines

00:07:18.810 --> 00:07:21.960
what people could have
done in order to jot down

00:07:21.960 --> 00:07:22.880
such a report.

00:07:22.880 --> 00:07:25.430
So let's look at this
first outline example.

00:07:25.430 --> 00:07:27.530
So this has four main points.

00:07:27.530 --> 00:07:29.880
First, the sizing of savings potential,

00:07:29.880 --> 00:07:32.650
so benchmark analysis,
activity-based sizing,

00:07:32.650 --> 00:07:34.230
results per business function.

00:07:34.230 --> 00:07:36.000
So in this first segment apparently,

00:07:36.000 --> 00:07:37.920
the social will propose to talk about,

00:07:37.920 --> 00:07:39.230
what the sizing was,

00:07:39.230 --> 00:07:41.270
what the identification
of the potential was.

00:07:41.270 --> 00:07:42.560
Then the second section is about,

00:07:42.560 --> 00:07:44.420
low hanging fruits measures.

00:07:44.420 --> 00:07:47.097
So in the area, production
sites and purchasing,

00:07:47.097 --> 00:07:50.030
now the low hanging fruits
measures are explained.

00:07:50.030 --> 00:07:51.500
Then the savings measures.

00:07:51.500 --> 00:07:54.280
So savings measures in
production, sales and purchasing,

00:07:54.280 --> 00:07:56.040
and then the proposed project plan

00:07:56.040 --> 00:07:57.750
would actually supposed to happen

00:07:57.750 --> 00:07:59.580
in order to bring this to life.

00:07:59.580 --> 00:08:01.630
So and again if you
just wanna take a moment

00:08:01.630 --> 00:08:02.463
to think about that,

00:08:02.463 --> 00:08:04.120
maybe also pause the video again.

00:08:04.120 --> 00:08:05.000
What do you think?

00:08:05.000 --> 00:08:07.230
what do you think about
this table of contents?

00:08:07.230 --> 00:08:08.620
Is this MECE?

00:08:08.620 --> 00:08:12.760
Do the elements here of this
progress report not overlap?

00:08:12.760 --> 00:08:14.830
So are they mutually exclusive,

00:08:14.830 --> 00:08:16.890
and are they collectively exhaustive?

00:08:16.890 --> 00:08:19.480
So do they cover all the key topics

00:08:19.480 --> 00:08:21.180
that you are supposed to talk about?

00:08:21.180 --> 00:08:23.790
And here with regards
to the MECE principle,

00:08:23.790 --> 00:08:26.370
I see at least two major problems.

00:08:26.370 --> 00:08:29.380
So the first problem is
regarding the first part.

00:08:29.380 --> 00:08:31.150
So mutually exclusive,

00:08:31.150 --> 00:08:32.300
and here in the sense,

00:08:32.300 --> 00:08:33.510
I believe it's pretty obvious,

00:08:33.510 --> 00:08:36.540
that for sure the sections two and three,

00:08:36.540 --> 00:08:39.640
they overlap because the
section three is called ,

00:08:39.640 --> 00:08:41.330
the savings measures,

00:08:41.330 --> 00:08:44.390
but section two is talking
about savings measures as well,

00:08:44.390 --> 00:08:46.270
because these low hanging fruits,

00:08:46.270 --> 00:08:49.020
they are savings measures as well, right?

00:08:49.020 --> 00:08:51.030
Maybe they are a bit of a
different type of measures,

00:08:51.030 --> 00:08:54.370
but for sure that should be
subsumed under savings measures.

00:08:54.370 --> 00:08:57.370
So here the sections two
and three, they overlap,

00:08:57.370 --> 00:08:58.750
they're not exclusive,

00:08:58.750 --> 00:09:00.830
which is why this is a logic error

00:09:00.830 --> 00:09:03.170
in structuring this progress report,

00:09:03.170 --> 00:09:05.290
it is a violation of the MECE principle.

00:09:05.290 --> 00:09:07.160
But there is a second violation as well,

00:09:07.160 --> 00:09:09.660
and this is now in regards
to the second element

00:09:09.660 --> 00:09:12.670
of MECE namely the collectively
exhausting element.

00:09:12.670 --> 00:09:15.160
Here there is something missing,

00:09:15.160 --> 00:09:17.350
and maybe if we'll
remember the project brief

00:09:17.350 --> 00:09:19.727
in the beginning, there was
a fourth segment as well,

00:09:19.727 --> 00:09:21.710
there was a fourth area,

00:09:21.710 --> 00:09:23.810
that you as a team are
supposed to look at,

00:09:23.810 --> 00:09:25.690
and this is now the overhead area.

00:09:25.690 --> 00:09:28.160
So besides production
sites and purchasing,

00:09:28.160 --> 00:09:30.630
the overhead segment needs
to be looked at as well,

00:09:30.630 --> 00:09:33.360
and apparently this is now
completely missing here.

00:09:33.360 --> 00:09:35.430
This is not talking
about overhead as well,

00:09:35.430 --> 00:09:38.630
so it's not complete, it's
not collectively exhaustive

00:09:38.630 --> 00:09:41.420
so this of course again
it's a second logic error

00:09:41.420 --> 00:09:42.840
when drafting this report.

00:09:42.840 --> 00:09:45.480
Now let's look into a
second outline example.

00:09:45.480 --> 00:09:48.230
And here now the associate
decided to structure it

00:09:48.230 --> 00:09:50.980
in five sub parts of the overall project.

00:09:50.980 --> 00:09:52.760
So first he wants to talk about the sizing

00:09:52.760 --> 00:09:53.900
of the savings potential,

00:09:53.900 --> 00:09:56.170
by talking about the conducted analysis

00:09:56.170 --> 00:09:58.510
and also the results
per business function.

00:09:58.510 --> 00:10:00.390
Then he has headers for all the areas

00:10:00.390 --> 00:10:01.830
for the functions he looked at,

00:10:01.830 --> 00:10:03.490
first production, then sales,

00:10:03.490 --> 00:10:05.510
and then he aggregated
purchasing and overhead,

00:10:05.510 --> 00:10:08.200
and he always first talks
about the short term measures

00:10:08.200 --> 00:10:09.830
and then the medium term measures.

00:10:09.830 --> 00:10:10.663
And then in the end,

00:10:10.663 --> 00:10:12.810
is where the proposed
project plan is coming up.

00:10:12.810 --> 00:10:14.910
So now again, pause the
video, think of Bowman.

00:10:14.910 --> 00:10:15.743
What do you think?

00:10:15.743 --> 00:10:18.140
Is this MECE or not?

00:10:18.140 --> 00:10:21.130
And I would not argue that,
yes, this is MECE, right?

00:10:21.130 --> 00:10:23.510
Because the way that he
chose to structure it here

00:10:23.510 --> 00:10:25.380
by looking area by area,

00:10:25.380 --> 00:10:28.450
this automatically makes it
mutually exclusive, right?

00:10:28.450 --> 00:10:30.140
So these do not overlap,

00:10:30.140 --> 00:10:32.030
and of course we're going to
discuss whether purchasing

00:10:32.030 --> 00:10:34.830
and all that shall be
aggregated in one area

00:10:34.830 --> 00:10:37.370
or whether you make two
distinct areas for them as well.

00:10:37.370 --> 00:10:39.730
But I would argue if these
are maybe smaller parts,

00:10:39.730 --> 00:10:41.440
it's fine to also put them together

00:10:41.440 --> 00:10:42.600
or also because purchasing

00:10:42.600 --> 00:10:44.540
and all that are maybe a bit more similar

00:10:44.540 --> 00:10:47.010
in terms of content compared
to production and sales,

00:10:47.010 --> 00:10:48.710
and then within each of these areas,

00:10:48.710 --> 00:10:51.800
the short term measures and
the medium term measures

00:10:51.800 --> 00:10:52.950
are distinguished

00:10:52.950 --> 00:10:54.810
and now these is a way of putting it

00:10:54.810 --> 00:10:56.480
where these now do not overlap

00:10:56.480 --> 00:10:59.060
because short term is of
course now a different horizon

00:10:59.060 --> 00:11:00.510
of measures that you look at

00:11:00.510 --> 00:11:02.090
compared to the medium term measures.

00:11:02.090 --> 00:11:04.680
So of course it would also
depend a bit on the content

00:11:04.680 --> 00:11:07.260
of what exactly is written
within each of these points,

00:11:07.260 --> 00:11:09.510
but overall this would be now a structure,

00:11:09.510 --> 00:11:12.070
at least I would argue
that, yes this is MECE,

00:11:12.070 --> 00:11:14.150
this might very well work for your report.

00:11:14.150 --> 00:11:17.620
And the reason why the MECE
principle is so important,

00:11:17.620 --> 00:11:20.450
is that whenever you
create a presentation,

00:11:20.450 --> 00:11:22.510
whenever you write a written report,

00:11:22.510 --> 00:11:23.381
and ideally also whenever
you talk about something

00:11:23.381 --> 00:11:27.270
in a structured and professional way,

00:11:27.270 --> 00:11:29.880
you should follow the MECE principle.

00:11:29.880 --> 00:11:33.400
You should structure your
reports, your presentations,

00:11:33.400 --> 00:11:37.220
and also your oral arguments
in a way that they are MECE,

00:11:37.220 --> 00:11:39.410
that they follow this MECE principle,

00:11:39.410 --> 00:11:41.350
because if you do not in most cases,

00:11:41.350 --> 00:11:43.310
your structure is flawed,

00:11:43.310 --> 00:11:44.143
there's a logic error

00:11:44.143 --> 00:11:46.830
in the way you're presenting your findings

00:11:46.830 --> 00:11:49.600
and of course you want to avoid
that in the business world.

00:11:49.600 --> 00:11:52.310
